Q: How to display an image with customized dimensions using CSS A: <p>If you want the image resized you need to resize the image it self not the div. 
You can either do:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;style&gt;
#myimg {
    width 10px;
    height: 10px;
}
&lt;/style&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Note on this second one it will target every div and image in the page. I recommend using an ID or Class to call the image</p>

<p>or:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;style&gt;
div img {
    width 10px;
    height: 10px;
}
&lt;/style&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>I just grabbed google logo for test</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div id="mydiv"&gt;&lt;img id="myimg" src="https://www.google.com/images/branding/googlelogo/1x/googlelogo_color_272x92dp.png" /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
